WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.886 --> 00:00:13.304
COLE: You ready to
reel a fish in, Willow?

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:14.973
WILLOW: Yeah.
COLE: It's been a while, huh?

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:17.600
WILLOW: Yeah.
COLE: We'll see.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:25.025
Well, today, Timber
and Willow, Willow mostly,

00:00:25.066 --> 00:00:27.569
they both been
asking to go fishing.

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:31.823
So, see if we can just
pull one winter king in.

00:00:32.907 --> 00:00:35.368
Kings, they got
good fat content,

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:37.787
especially this time of year.

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:39.372
Oh, and we don't get sunshine.

00:00:39.414 --> 00:00:41.666
Salmon's our Vitamin D.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:45.170
Oh, yeah, I'm
starting to mark bait.

00:00:46.004 --> 00:00:47.922
Timber, are you okay
to drive for a minute?

00:00:47.964 --> 00:00:49.382
TIMBER: Yeah.

00:00:49.424 --> 00:00:51.593
COLE: You drive and
I'll throw out the,

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:54.512
the sneaker pole
out the back here.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:57.474
See if we can't get
these girls hooked on a king.

00:00:57.515 --> 00:00:59.225
TIMBER: Cross your fingers!

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:01.770
COLE: I am Cole Sturgis.

00:01:01.811 --> 00:01:04.856
I live in Thorne Bay, Alaska
on Prince of Wales Island.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:07.400
In Southeast Alaska.

00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:11.196
My family and I live in
our two-story house that

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.073
floats in the ocean.

00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:14.699
My oldest is Timber.

00:01:14.699 --> 00:01:16.785
My middle daughter is Willow,

00:01:16.826 --> 00:01:19.871
and we have a little
two-year-old that's, uh, Cedar.

00:01:19.871 --> 00:01:20.955
And when you're a logger,

00:01:20.997 --> 00:01:23.083
you tend to name
your kids after trees.

00:01:23.124 --> 00:01:24.751
(laughs)

00:01:25.293 --> 00:01:28.379
Coming from Montana, I've
never been in the ocean really.

00:01:28.379 --> 00:01:32.509
Until I found a
job cutting timber.

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:36.179
And didn't take us
long at all to figure out

00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:38.056
we're heading North.

00:01:41.059 --> 00:01:44.104
For me, everything
in Thorne Bay's unique.

00:01:44.395 --> 00:01:46.564
The peace, the quiet of it.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:49.025
There's no rat race here.

00:01:50.568 --> 00:01:52.237
It's a rainforest.

00:01:52.237 --> 00:01:55.573
Things grow here
like I've never seen.

00:01:56.241 --> 00:01:58.618
It's a magical place.

00:02:00.078 --> 00:02:04.666
We try to sustain on
what the ocean gives us.

00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:07.919
And this land
around here provides us.

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:11.256
If we don't stay on
top of the food chain,

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.258
we starve.

00:02:14.092 --> 00:02:17.428
To be proficient up here,
you have to be stubborn.

00:02:18.054 --> 00:02:22.058
I'm kind of a jack of all
trades and a master of none.

00:02:22.433 --> 00:02:24.602
I don't know much,
but I know a lot.

00:02:24.602 --> 00:02:26.563
You know?

00:02:26.771 --> 00:02:28.982
Nice and easy. There you go.

00:02:29.023 --> 00:02:30.608
TIMBER: We're under one.

00:02:30.608 --> 00:02:32.777
COLE: Good job.

00:02:34.112 --> 00:02:37.365
It's a big advantage, teaching
your children how to drive.

00:02:37.407 --> 00:02:39.826
I can be manning the poles.

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:42.745
Timber knows to
take us on course.

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:48.293
Need one now
we're just waiting now.

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:51.212
Good job, girls.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.591
Really makes a person proud.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:59.179
That your
children are that cool.

00:03:00.305 --> 00:03:01.973
Yeah, good duck coming in.

00:03:01.973 --> 00:03:04.058
Let's see if
there's a king in here.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.352
TIMBER: Yeah, I like that.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.106
COLE: This is the greatest
thing I've been gifted with.

00:03:10.148 --> 00:03:12.483
To raise my girls.

00:03:12.483 --> 00:03:15.236
And help them and teach them.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:24.746
(gusting winds)

00:03:28.166 --> 00:03:31.169
(shivering)

00:03:31.169 --> 00:03:32.670
COLE: What's wrong, Willow?

00:03:36.132 --> 00:03:38.718
COLE: Timber, you're cold?
TIMBER: Yeah.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:41.346
COLE: All right, we'll
circle back towards the house.

00:03:41.346 --> 00:03:43.181
I'll just go out
and check tomorrow,

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.891
maybe we'll get some fish.

